From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitPlay <splitplay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:02:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] splitplay: serve the worker's own session, not the console

Upstream Sunshine assumes it serves the active console session:
retrieve_users_token() asks WTSGetActiveConsoleSessionId() for the session
whose user token launches apps and prep commands. A SplitPlay worker runs
as SYSTEM with TokenSessionId set to its desk's RDP loopback session, so
the console is the wrong session (and usually another user).

Add platf::target_session_id(), which returns the session of the worker
process itself (ProcessIdToSessionId), and use it in
retrieve_users_token(). This was the only WTSGetActiveConsoleSessionId()
call in src/ at the pinned commit; tools/sunshinesvc.cpp also uses it but
is not part of the worker.

Input (SendInput/OpenInputDesktop), DXGI capture and WASAPI already act
on the calling process's session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J21Rm42dakZVfEnnyh7aQn

diff --git a/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp b/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp
index eb0cda7c8966eac40fe282e115e8125855cc37d6..aae501198ac6e997081e0d47413c2c7ad9deb84a 100644
--- a/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp
+++ b/src/platform/windows/misc.cpp
@@ -291,6 +291,23 @@ namespace platf {
     return ret;
   }
 
+  /**
+   * @brief Session whose user the worker serves.
+   *
+   * SplitPlay: upstream Sunshine serves the active console session. The SplitPlay worker is started by the
+   * service with TokenSessionId set to its desk's (RDP loopback) session, so it serves its own session instead.
+   *
+   * @return Session id of the current process, or 0xFFFFFFFF on failure.
+   */
+  DWORD target_session_id() {
+    DWORD session_id = 0xFFFFFFFF;
+    if (!ProcessIdToSessionId(GetCurrentProcessId(), &session_id)) {
+      BOOST_LOG(error) << "ProcessIdToSessionId failed: "sv << GetLastError();
+      return 0xFFFFFFFF;
+    }
+    return session_id;
+  }
+
   /**
    * @brief Obtain the current sessions user's primary token with elevated privileges.
    * @return The user's token. If user has admin capability it will be elevated, otherwise it will be a limited token. On error, `nullptr`.
@@ -303,15 +320,15 @@ namespace platf {
     TOKEN_ELEVATION_TYPE elevationType;
     DWORD dwSize;
 
-    // Get the session ID of the active console session
-    consoleSessionId = WTSGetActiveConsoleSessionId();
+    // SplitPlay: use the worker's own session, not the active console session
+    consoleSessionId = target_session_id();
     if (0xFFFFFFFF == consoleSessionId) {
-      // If there is no active console session, log a warning and return null
+      // If there is no session, log a warning and return null
       BOOST_LOG(warning) << "There isn't an active user session, therefore it is not possible to execute commands under the users profile.";
       return nullptr;
     }
 
-    // Get the user token for the active console session
+    // Get the user token for the worker's session
     if (!WTSQueryUserToken(consoleSessionId, &userToken)) {
       BOOST_LOG(debug) << "QueryUserToken failed, this would prevent commands from launching under the users profile.";
       return nullptr;
